    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="A simple closed polygon splits the plane into an inside and an outside (the Jordan curve theorem). A ray cast from a point crosses the boundary an odd number of times exactly when the point is inside. The crossings are found edge by edge with segment_intersection, and their parity agrees with point_in_polygon on a concave, spiral-like polygon.">

